  "comment": {
   "comments": [
    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "5fca8bc90d2f61006fc5ed4f",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": false,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/21ba258a751aa2077b4f25047d85b5c4?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FA-6.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/21ba258a751aa2077b4f25047d85b5c4?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FA-6.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/21ba258a751aa2077b4f25047d85b5c4?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FA-6.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/21ba258a751aa2077b4f25047d85b5c4?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FA-6.png"
      },
      "displayName": "asconrad",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=5fca8bc90d2f61006fc5ed4f",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "As a colleague of James I have done further research.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "The FOXML file that is being ingested, sifd_1058.xml, has been generated by fedora-export.sh from another Fedora repository. The problem seems to be the last datastream definition in that that file:",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "<foxml:datastream CONTROL_GROUP=\"M\" ID=\"provenanceMetadata\" STATE=\"A\" VERSIONABLE=\"true\">",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "<foxml:datastreamVersion CREATED=\"2013-07-17T08:29:40.294Z\" ID=\"provenanceMetadata.0\" LABEL=\"\" MIMETYPE=\"text/xml\" SIZE=\"53\">",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "<foxml:contentLocation",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "REF=\"",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "marks": [
           {
            "attrs": {
             "href": "http://localhost:8080/fedora/get/sifd:1058/provenanceMetadata/2013-07-17T08:29:40.294Z"
            },
            "type": "link"
           }
          ],
          "text": "http://localhost:8080/fedora/get/sifd:1058/provenanceMetadata/2013-07-17T08:29:40.294Z",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "text": "\" TYPE=\"INTERNAL_ID\"/>",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "</foxml:datastreamVersion>",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "</foxml:datastream>",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "The problem is the \"REF\" statement as the fedora-import command seems to try to execute that \"get\" before the object has actually been created. Import works by removing the datastream in question (CONTROL_GROUP=\"M\") from the FOXML file. Probably not a good idea, though... ",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "I am not a Fedora export so it is hard to assess whether this is a bug, or rather a consequence of our data model.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
