  "comment": {
   "comments": [
    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "5fca8bc90d2f61006fc5ed4f",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": false,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/21ba258a751aa2077b4f25047d85b5c4?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FA-6.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/21ba258a751aa2077b4f25047d85b5c4?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FA-6.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/21ba258a751aa2077b4f25047d85b5c4?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FA-6.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/21ba258a751aa2077b4f25047d85b5c4?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FA-6.png"
      },
      "displayName": "asconrad",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=5fca8bc90d2f61006fc5ed4f",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>As a colleague of James I have done further research.</p>\n\n<p>The FOXML file that is being ingested, sifd_1058.xml, has been generated by fedora-export.sh from another Fedora repository. The problem seems to be the last datastream definition in that that file:</p>\n\n<p>  &lt;foxml:datastream CONTROL_GROUP=\"M\" ID=\"provenanceMetadata\" STATE=\"A\" VERSIONABLE=\"true\"&gt;<br/>\n    &lt;foxml:datastreamVersion CREATED=\"2013-07-17T08:29:40.294Z\" ID=\"provenanceMetadata.0\" LABEL=\"\" MIMETYPE=\"text/xml\" SIZE=\"53\"&gt;<br/>\n      &lt;foxml:contentLocation<br/>\n        REF=\"http://localhost:8080/fedora/get/sifd:1058/provenanceMetadata/2013-07-17T08:29:40.294Z\" TYPE=\"INTERNAL_ID\"/&gt;<br/>\n    &lt;/foxml:datastreamVersion&gt;<br/>\n  &lt;/foxml:datastream&gt;</p>\n\n<p>The problem is the \"REF\" statement as the fedora-import command seems to try to execute that \"get\" before the object has actually been created. Import works by removing the datastream in question (CONTROL_GROUP=\"M\") from the FOXML file. Probably not a good idea, though... </p>\n\n<p>I am not a Fedora export so it is hard to assess whether this is a bug, or rather a consequence of our data model.</p>",
     "created": "25/Jul/13 4:28 PM",
     "id": "12536",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/11194/comment/12536",
